# Pub versions and modern Flutter/Dart APIs

## Pub package versions

- Before adding or bumping a dependency in `pubspec.yaml`, look up the **current** stable version on pub.dev. Prefer `user-dart` `pub_dev_search`, `dart pub add`, or a live fetch — never invent or reuse stale versions from memory.
- Prefer caret constraints (`^x.y.z`) matching the latest stable release unless this project already uses a different constraint style.
- After changing deps, run `flutter pub get` (or `dart pub get`) and fix resolution issues.

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — guessed / remembered version
dependencies:
  http: ^0.13.0

# ✅ GOOD — version confirmed from pub.dev just now
dependencies:
  http: ^1.2.2
```

## Modern APIs only

- Use current Flutter/Dart stable APIs only. Do not introduce deprecated members, Material 2-only patterns when Material 3 is the project default, or obsolete packages when a maintained replacement exists.
- When unsure an API is current, verify with package docs or Dart MCP (`read_package_uris`, `analyze_files`) — do not guess.
- Prefer null-safe, modern language features already used in the repo (records, patterns, sealed classes, etc.) when they fit existing style. Do not regress to pre-null-safety or deprecated patterns.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — deprecated API
ThemeData(primarySwatch: Colors.blue);

// ✅ GOOD — current Material 3 API
ThemeData(
  colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: Colors.blue),
  useMaterial3: true,
);
```
